{
 "description": "Common-postprocessor diagnostic for every saved DNS velocity field.\n\nThe Section 8 headline comparisons previously measured each route's dissipation\nand peak vorticity through that route's own derivative operator. When the thesis\nis that one operator has the sharper numerical wavenumber, measuring the fields\nthrough the operator being judged is circular. This script removes the bias: one\nFourier postprocessor, identical for every scheme, applied to the raw saved\nvelocity fields.\n\nFor each dump in code/solver/data/{tgvfield,reconfield}_*.bin (x-fastest layout,\nu then v then w, read as C-order [z,y,x]; box [0,2pi)^3) it computes, with the\nexact spectral curl:\n\n  * unfiltered: E = <|u|^2>/2, Z = <|omega|^2>/2, eps_ens = 2 nu Z, max|omega|;\n  * 2/3-bandlimited: the same after the pseudospectral reference's dealias mask\n    (|k_axis| <= (2/3)(N/2), the mask in ps_reference.py), which measures the\n    resolved-band content and discards grid-edge aliasing debris.\n\nThe dump time is inferred by inverting the run's own monotone E(t) history from\nits CSV at the field's (operator-free) energy, which simultaneously checks that\nthe saved field and the CSV agree. TGV records also carry the van Rees 512^3\nworkshop reference (psref/spectral_Re1600_512.gdiag) interpolated to the dump\ntime, so percent-of-reference is like-for-like in time; reconnection records\nnormalize peak vorticity by the same common diagnostic of that run's own t0\ndump. Native CSV values are recorded alongside to quantify the operator-native\nbias. Output: code/results/s8_common_diagnostic.json.",
 "conventions": {
  "box": "[0,2pi)^3",
  "layout": "[z,y,x] x-fastest",
  "dealias_mask": "|k_axis| <= (2/3)(N/2) per axis (ps_reference.py)",
  "eps_ens": "nu * <|omega|^2> = 2 nu Z",
  "E": "<|u|^2>/2"
 },
 "reference": {
  "file": "psref/spectral_Re1600_512.gdiag",
  "peak_eps": 0.012857528187,
  "t_peak": 8.97
 },
